SUMMARY:Heels Class with Masha (4
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T203000
UID:2609230P-4028QaUiSS6Ndv2tqrQ
DESCRIPTION:October 12 – November 2\n\nHeels Class — Open to All Level
 s\n\nStep into your confidence and learn the foundations of dancing in hee
 ls in a supportive\, no-pressure environment. This class is designed for b
 eginners and anyone looking to build strength\, balance\, and style from t
 he ground up.\n\nWhat to Expect:\n\n• The Fundamentals: Learn how to bal
 ance\, walk\, and groove safely and confidently.\n\n• Empowering Choreog
 raphy: Dive into a fun\, expressive routine that celebrates your unique st
 yle.\n\n• A Supportive Community: Dance alongside a non-judgmental group
  focused on self-expression\n\nWe’ll focus on this heels class:\n\n– W
 alking with confidence and control\n\n– Basic technique\, posture\, and 
 lines\n\n– Musicality and rhythm\n\n– Simple choreography to help you 
 feel expressive and empowered\n\nExpect a fun\, encouraging space where yo
 u can explore your femininity\, build body awareness\, and grow at your ow
 n pace. No experience needed—just bring your energy and a pair of heels 
 you feel comfortable in \\(or start in socks!\\).\n\nAll levels welcome. C
 ome as you are\n\n4-weeks \, October 12 – November 2\n\nEarly bird price
  $100\, at the door $130\n\nMonday 7:30 PM – 8:30 PM
LOCATION:Salsa Dance Marin
URL:https://salsadancemarin.com/heels-with-masha/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.srsymphony.org/event/twist-of-fate/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.srsymphony.org/event/twist-of-fate/", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/twist-of-fate-2/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.srsymphony.org/event/twist-of-fate/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Twist of Fate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T213000
UID:260529NsHyOVVEpUG5RUEq-_miLg
DESCRIPTION:Twist of Fate\n\nOctober 10\, 11 & 12\, 2026\n\nWeill Hall\, G
 reen Music Center\n\nFrancesco Lecce-Chong\, conductor\n\nMaxim Lando\, pi
 ano\n\nMATT BROWNE: Divertimento for Orchestra \\(World Premiere\\) FRANZ 
 LISZT: Concerto No. 1 in E-Flat major for Piano and Orchestra\, S.124 PYOT
 R ILYICH TCHAIKOVSKY: Symphony No. 4 in F minor\, Opus 36\n\nThe season’
 s opener begins with a fanfare of fate\, which marks a poignant full circl
 e for Francesco Lecce-Chong. He returns to the first piece he led with the
  Symphony: Tchaikovsky’s tempestuous Symphony No. 4. This high-octane pr
 ogram also features fiery virtuoso Maxim Lando in Liszt’s thrilling Pian
 o Concerto No. 1 and a world premiere by Matt Browne\, a celebrated alumnu
 s of the First Symphony Project.\n\nPrograms\, dates\, artists\, and price
 s are subject to change without notice. Tickets are subject to availabilit
 y.\n\nPhoto by Chris McGuire
LOCATION:Green Music Center
URL:https://www.srsymphony.org/event/twist-of-fate/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
