SUMMARY:Alibi LGBTQ+ October Book Club: "The Passion" by Jeanette Winterso
 n
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261014T173000
UID:261003Q8R-iA3dTk-uklGe2psq1Q
DESCRIPTION:Please join us Wednesday\, October 14th for our LGBTQ\\+ Book 
 Club’s discussion of Jeanette Winterson’s classic\, “The Passion\,
 ” hosted by Richard May. Set during the tumultuous years of the Nepoleon
 ic Wars\, The Passion intertwines the destinies of two remarkable people: 
 Henri\, a simple French soldier\, who follow Napoleon from glory to Russia
 n ruin\; and Villanelle\, a red-haired\, web-footed daughter of a Venetian
  boatman\, whose husband has gambled away her heart. In Venice’s compoun
 d of carnival\, chance\, and darkness\, the pair meet their singular desti
 ny. In her unique and mesmerizing voice\, Winterson blends reality with fa
 ntasy\, dream\, and imagination to weave a hypnotic take with stunning eff
 ects. Books are available in the shop\, online including ebook at bookshop
 .org/shop/alibibookshop
LOCATION:Anchor Pantry
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/2296206047844488/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
