SUMMARY:Marin Farmers Markets
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T130000
UID:260924xtylTy3zs02znBcYG28K9g
DESCRIPTION:Price: Free\n\nSponsor: Marin Center\n\nExplore the bounty of 
 summer at the Marin Farmers Markets. Taste vine-ripened tomatoes\, corn th
 at was picked that morning\, and peaches so juicy you have to bend over ju
 st to get a bite. Farm-fresh eggs\, grass-fed beef\, artisan c heeses\, ra
 w milk\, and freshly baked breads complete the shopping exper ience. Speci
 alty prepared foods and handmade art add to the magic of the market.\n\nEn
 joy the intimate feeling of the Thursday Marin Farmers Market\, an ideal p
 lace to meet for lunch and pick up fresh produce for the weekend. Discover
  the abundance and diversity of product at the celebrated Sunday Marin Far
 mers Market\, the third largest farmers market in California. Turn your do
 llar into a vote for local sustainable agriculture\, shrink your eco-footp
 rint\, and revive the feeling of being intimate ly connected to your food 
 by meeting your farmers face-to-face. The market takes place rain or shine
 .\n\nwww.aginstitutemarin.org
LOCATION:Marin Veterans' Memorial Auditorium
URL:https://www.marincounty.gov/county-marin-calendar
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs", "Press Democrat": "https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Antarctica: The Frozen Desert | Photographs by Vegar Abelsnes
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T170000
UID:260914HrNT_wMhi0mJHstT7Mc_Kw
DESCRIPTION:1st Street Gallery at WTRSHD will present “Antarctica: The F
 rozen Desert\,” a new body of fine art photography by Vegar Abelsnes\, o
 pening September 26th\, 2026\, and on view September through November.  T
 he exhibition marks a deliberate turn in Abelsnes’ photography\; after m
 ore than two decades of working in a commercial and advertising capacity\,
  he has embarked on a career as a photo and field guide in the polar regio
 ns. The exhibit features work generated over 6 voyages to the Antarctic Pe
 ninsula. He is returning to Antarctica in January and will add the Falklan
 ds and South Georgia to his list of destinations to guide and photograph.\
 n\nTraveling to some of the most remote and inhospitable coastlines on Ear
 th\, Abelsnes has photographed a landscape that exists almost entirely out
 side of human time. The ice in these images began forming millions of year
 s ago\, while Homo sapiens have only existed for roughly 300\,000 years. D
 efined by such a scale\, Antarctica is less a place than a record — vast
 \, indifferent\, treacherous\, and staggeringly beautiful\, holding a kind
  of cosmic truth that Abelsnes says is more important now than ever before
 .
LOCATION:1st Street Gallery @ WTRSHD
URL:https://vegarabelsnes.com/ANTARCTICA:-The-Frozen-Desert/thumbs
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
