BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/the-addams-family", "Press Democrat": "https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/the-addams-family"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/the-addams-family"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Addams Family Musical
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T220000
UID:261005qDI80P8hAE-zPWf6nxe85A
DESCRIPTION:San Marin Performing Arts is kicking off the 2026–27 season 
 with The Addams Family\, a delightfully spooky musical coming to the Emily
  Gates Performing Arts Center\n\nJust in time for Halloween\, this family-
 friendly production brings the famously eccentric Addams family to the sta
 ge in a story filled with humor\, heart\, memorable music and plenty of wo
 nderfully macabre fun. In The Addams Family\, Wednesday Addams has grown u
 p—and fallen in love with a sweet\, smart young man from a perfectly “
 normal” family. When she invites him and his parents to dinner\, Wednesd
 ay asks Gomez to keep a secret from Morticia\, setting off a hilarious cha
 in of events that turns one unforgettable evening upside down.\n\nFamily f
 riendly show!\n\nOUR STUDENT CAST\n\nGomez Addams — Kaden Hockinson\n\nM
 orticia Addams — Cami Cabrera\n\nWednesday Addams — Aaliyah Ortiz\n\nP
 ugsley Addams — Rosie Chi\n\nUncle Fester — Rogan Ferrell Bell\n\nGran
 dma Addams — Lenore Schulz\n\nLurch — Wyatt Mathyssen\n\nLucas Beineke
  — Skyler Viola\n\nMal Beineke — Tobias Mossberger\n\nAlice Beineke 
 — Clara Rose\n\nThe Ancestors — Hannah Yako\, Ella Blok\, Kody Kong\, 
 Noemy Pineda Montiel\, Dasha Hirai\, Maya Geere\, Sophia Gomez
LOCATION:Emily Gates Performing Arts Center
URL:https://www.sanmarinperformingarts.org/news-highlights/the-addams-fami
 ly
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomavalleyhistory.org/event/joseph-hooker-sonoma-valleys-soldier-gambler-farmer/", "Press Democrat": "https://sonomavalleyhistory.org/event/joseph-hooker-sonoma-valleys-soldier-gambler-farmer/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sonomavalleyhistory.org/event/joseph-hooker-sonoma-valleys-soldier-gambler-farmer/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Joseph Hooker: Sonoma Valley's Soldier\, Gambler\, & Farmer
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T201500
UID:260909ijTEPIZ70Uqo10yX9fAl2Q
DESCRIPTION:Joseph Hooker is remembered in history as a complex and highly
  controversial military figure. Understanding his past helps explain his f
 uture and his decisions.\n\nBefore gaining national fame as the commander 
 of the Union’s famous Army of the Potomac\, he faced both professional a
 nd personal struggles in Sonoma Valley\, many of which he caused himself. 
 During his time in Sonoma\, his well-known ego\, brashness\, and questiona
 ble dealings led to a series of costly mistakes that would follow him into
  the Civil War.\n\nJoin us for a fascinating presentation by author Travis
  P. Wagner. He will share new information on “Fighting Joe” Hooker’s
  turbulent years in Sonoma Valley. His talk will explore the complex man b
 ehind the myth. It will cover his time as a military officer\, a high-stak
 es gambler\, and a struggling frontier farmer\, before he achieved fame in
  the Civil War.\n\nTravis P. Wagner is a Professor Emeritus at the Univers
 ity of Southern Maine. He earned his Ph.D. from The George Washington Univ
 ersity. Dr. Wagner has written numerous articles on the history of America
 n industry\, environmental policy\, and technology. His eighth book\, Mili
 tary Honor on Trial: The Saga of Joseph Hooker and George H. Derby\, was p
 ublished by Sequoia Grove Press in August.
LOCATION:Sonoma Community Center - Community Room 110
URL:https://sonomavalleyhistory.org/event/joseph-hooker-sonoma-valleys-sol
 dier-gambler-farmer/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.facebook.com/events/1759417791635789/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Alibi Bookshop's Memoir Book Club: "Behind the Desk at the Main
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T190000
UID:261003N52maJ4OhEmIxoIQTprplg
DESCRIPTION:Banned Books Week is October 4-10th\, but we’ll be continuin
 g the observance on Thursday\, October 15th at 7pm by discussing “Behind
  the Desk at the Main: A Librarian’s Memoir” by local author and icon\
 , Dorothy Lazard\, who knows all too well about banned books. From a celeb
 rated librarian and public historian\, a memoir about the promise of publi
 c libraries in a fractured world. “This wonderful book appeals to the he
 art as well as to the mind\, challenging the dark times we live in.” —
 Azar Nafisi\, author of author of Read Dangerously and Reading Lolita in T
 ehran When Dorothy Lazard became a public librarian\, she returned to the 
 building that had shaped her life from childhood. At the flagship branch \
 \(“the Main”\\) of the Oakland Public Library\, she connected with her
  hometown to a degree that few people experience. Helping her fellow commu
 nity members and ultimately becoming the keeper of Oakland’s public hist
 ory archives\, she witnessed the joys and dilemmas that shape one of the m
 ost diverse cities in the US. In Behind the Desk at the Main\, Lazard take
 s readers through the day-to-day life of library work with love\, wit\, an
 d candor. As the cracks in American society grow and our public institutio
 ns are strained to the breaking point\, libraries remain the cherished con
 tainers of our ideals: They are places of curiosity\, imagination\, memory
 \, and togetherness. Lazard reveals the pressures that library workers fac
 e—from economic crises to book bans and political upheaval—as they uph
 old these ideals in a fractured world. Filled with humor and urgency\, Beh
 ind the Desk at the Main is a testament to the power of books and communit
 y in a time of division. Books are available in the shop — Dorothy will 
 actually be here on September 19th at 4pm so you can come and meet her and
  get one signed! Also available online and ebook: bookshop.org/shop/alibib
 ookshop
LOCATION:Anchor Pantry
URL:https://www.facebook.com/events/1759417791635789/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
