UID:261004okJolO6oekyNZiGjds7gug
DESCRIPTION:Join Jack London Park Partners and Sonoma Ecology Center staff
  in a series of intermediate hikes\, guided in Spanish\, between Jack Lond
 on State Historic Park and Sugarloaf Ridge State Park. Each hike is a roun
 d trip\, returning to the starting point\, and will increase in length or 
 difficulty. Not appropriate for children under 12 years old.\n\nSat. Oct. 
 17 – Sugarloaf's waterfall loop. 2.39 miles\, 610 ft. elevation \\(meet 
 at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\\).\n\nSat. Oct. 24 – Upper Fallen to Camp
  Via to Fern Lake at Jack London. 5.72 miles\, 1\,150 ft. elevation \\(mee
 t at Jack London State Historic Park\\).\n\nSat. Nov. 7 – Gunsight Rock 
 at Sugarloaf/Hood Mountain Regional Park. 6.44 miles\, 2\,129 ft. elevatio
 n \\(meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\\).\n\nSun. Nov. 15 – Sonoma Rid
 ge in Sonoma Developmental Center/Jack London. 9.67 miles\, 2\,126 ft. ele
 vation \\(meet at the intersection of Arnold Dr. and Harney Rd.\, inside t
 he SDC\\).\n\nSat.  Nov. 21 – "The Big Loop" at Sugarloaf. 7.37 miles\,
  1\,739 ft elevation \\(meet at Sugarloaf Ridge State Park\\).
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/reto2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
