 udio**. Experiment with mark-making and suminagashi a Japanese paper marbl
 ing technique\, and create your own artwork to take home. No experience is
  needed\, and all materials are provided.\n\nSGVCC will also be introducin
 g their **New Fall Classes\, After-School Enrichment Programs\, Creative T
 ry-Outs\, and the Figure Drawing Studio**.\n\nThe **Maker Space Opening** 
 is designed for all ages\, though young children should be accompanied by 
 an adult. Suggested donation: $25 per person\, with all proceeds supporti
 ng the Community Center’s arts programming. Light refreshments will be s
 erved.\n\nCome get creative\, explore the new space\, and discover what’
 s ahead at the Maker Space! We hope to see you at the Center soon!\n\nQues
 tions? Contact: dfogel@sgvcc.org
