BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/the-embodied-mind-js1d26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/the-embodied-mind-js1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/the-embodied-mind-js1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:The Embodied Mind: The Somatic Language of Thoughts and Emotions
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T150000
UID:260909hRIlAHnYOUmebYAW3xuFdA
DESCRIPTION:with Jill Satterfield\n\nEmerging research on the predictive a
 spect of the nervous system suggests the body doesn’t just react to our 
 thoughts and emotions — it can and does anticipate them\, generating pre
 dictions that may shape what we’re about to feel and think even before w
 e’ve consciously registered it. The hair rising on the back of your neck
 \, a gut feeling before you know why: these are signs of the nervous syste
 m registering and responding to signals caring for us\, before they’ve b
 een consciously processed as thought or story. What we experience as spont
 aneous is often the tail end of a process that began in the body moments e
 arlier. This daylong workshop trains attention on that predictive layer an
 d develops interoception\, or internal awareness\, the felt sense arising 
 in real time prior to story or interpretation. We’ll explore meditation 
 and mindfulness practices along with self – guided breathing as a bridge
  between body and mind — to build sensitivity to early signals of the ra
 w data that the nervous system is constantly generating. Through breathwor
 k and nervous-system-informed relaxation techniques\, we’ll practice int
 ervening at the point of origin\, where there is still room to choose a di
 fferent response rather than being carried by a habit reaction\, already s
 et in motion.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/the-embodied-mind-js1d
 26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
