SUMMARY:Centering Trust: Building Mental Health Access for Undocumented St
 udents
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T100000
DTSTAMP:20261008T112214Z
UID:20261020T160000Z-24104@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T090000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,900,900/716_c_square_Undocu-Immigrant-Logo-Pattern-J
 H.rev.1788894273.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:Undocumented students face significant mental health needs yet
  remain underserved due to immigration-related barriers and gaps in how in
 stitutions provide support. Research from Immigrants Rising's mental healt
 h programs reveals that trust – at both the institutional and interperso
 nal levels – is a critical missing condition. This session presents find
 ings from our research\, identifies best practices\, and offers concrete\,
  adaptable models for collaboration among campus and community stakeholder
 s. Participants will leave with practical next steps.  Viewing party at PA
 U Center - Bertolini 3rd Floor\, #4832Registration though Zoom. (https://f
 oundationccc-org.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_iIn25KloTQ-VzVnIDjFbZQ#/regis
 tration)For more information about Undocumented Student Success Week\, vis
 it the Undocu · Immigrant · Dream Center website. (https://dream.santaro
 sa.edu/workshops-events-2026-2027)
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T182214Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/24104-centering-trust-building-me
 ntal-health-access-for
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Undocumented students face significant m
 ental health needs yet remain underserved due to immigration-related barri
 ers and gaps in how institutions provide support. Research from Immigrants
  Rising's mental health programs reveals that trust – at both the instit
 utional and interpersonal levels – is a critical missing condition. This
  session presents findings from our research\, identifies best practices\,
  and offers concrete\, adaptable models for collaboration among campus and
  community stakeholders. Participants will leave with practical next steps
 .</p><p>  Viewing party at PAU Center - Bertolini 3rd Floor\, #4832</p><p>
 <strong><a href="https://foundationccc-org.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_iIn
 25KloTQ-VzVnIDjFbZQ#/registration" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Registra
 tion though Zoom.</a></strong></p><p><a href="https://dream.santarosa.edu/
 workshops-events-2026-2027" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more inform
 ation about Undocumented Student Success Week\, visit the Undocu · Immigr
 ant · Dream Center website.</a></p>
