X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sandra von Arb\, co-author of Dragonflies (Anisoptera) of Californ
 ia
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261020T210000
UID:261005-BiJBEf--U2JEntM6HsihA
DESCRIPTION:Learn about colorful and interesting dragonflies and their uni
 que biology with field biologist Sandra von Arb\, co-author of *Dragonflie
 s (Anisoptera) of California* with Kathy Biggs. Sandra will share her know
 ledge of the 47 species that occur here\, how to identify them\, what the 
 dragonflies need for survival\, where to find them\, and their migratory h
 abits.\n\nSandra von Arb has been a professional wildlife biologist for 30
  years\, focusing on sensitive and endangered species in northern Californ
 ia\, southern Oregon\, and northern Illinois. She is a co-founder of Biodi
 versity Education and Research Foundation\, whose mission is to foster eco
 logical stewardship through science and education.
LOCATION:Luther Burbank Art and Garden Center
URL:http://www.chapters.cnps.org/milobaker/events-and-activities/general-m
 eeting-speaker-series/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
