DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T130000
UID:261004vfc8G7ronEiAi0lLtq1LcA
DESCRIPTION:The Santa Rosa Community Farmers' Market on Wednesdays is a cu
 rated selection of the best Sonoma County and the surrounding region has t
 o offer. We are dedicated to championing local food\, agriculture\, and ar
 t. Our mission is to elevate local artisans\, farmers\, and producers whil
 e supporting the diverse communities that embrace them. Established in 196
 7 and currently managed by Agricultural Community Events Farmers' Market\,
  we hold ourselves to the exceptional high standard that comes with the ro
 le of every Certified California Farmers Market.
LOCATION:Santa Rosa Veteran's Memorial Building
URL:https://www.ilovefarmersmarkets.org/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Formative Influence Art Exhibit
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T160000
UID:2609093ztFi3mK9UCND6zxB09x_g
DESCRIPTION:Formative Influence explores the transformative power of light
  across five bodies of work. Inspired by the landscapes of Northern Califo
 rnia and the American West\, the exhibition examines the shift from photog
 raphy\, where light is observed and captured\, to painting\, where light i
 s created to shape new visual experiences. Rather than documenting the lan
 dscape\, these works evoke its emotional resonance\, emphasizing atmospher
 e\, memory\, and perception over literal representation.
LOCATION:Marin Center
URL:https://www.marincultural.org/exhibitions
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
