SUMMARY:More Than a Starting Point: The Power of Noncredit Education for U
 ndocumented Students
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T090000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T100000
DTSTAMP:20261008T113327Z
UID:20261021T160000Z-24105@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T090000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,900,900/716_c_square_Undocu-Immigrant-Logo-Pattern-J
 H.rev.1788894273.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:Noncredit education can provide an important pathway for undoc
 umented and immigration impacted students to access higher education\, bui
 ld skills\, and advance toward their academic and career goals. This webin
 ar will highlight promising practices for creating welcoming and inclusive
  noncredit programs\, supporting students as they navigate AB 540 eligibil
 ity\, strengthening partnerships across campus and community\, and buildin
 g pathways from noncredit to credit programs. Presenters will share practi
 cal strategies and lessons from the field that colleges can adapt to stren
 gthen access\, belonging\, retention\, and student success.  Viewing party
  at PAU Center - Bertolini 3rd Floor\, #4832Registration though Zoom. (htt
 ps://foundationccc-org.zoom.us/webinar/register/WN_j5g13fG9SDyN4njwBP8EUg#
 /registration)For more information about Undocumented Student Success Week
 \, visit the Undocu · Immigrant · Dream Center website. (https://dream.s
 antarosa.edu/workshops-events-2026-2027)
LAST-MODIFIED:20261008T185118Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/event/24105-more-than-a-starting-point-
 the-power-of-noncredit
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Noncredit education can provide an impor
 tant pathway for undocumented and immigration impacted students to access 
 higher education\, build skills\, and advance toward their academic and ca
 reer goals. This webinar will highlight promising practices for creating w
 elcoming and inclusive noncredit programs\, supporting students as they na
 vigate AB 540 eligibility\, strengthening partnerships across campus and c
 ommunity\, and building pathways from noncredit to credit programs. Presen
 ters will share practical strategies and lessons from the field that colle
 ges can adapt to strengthen access\, belonging\, retention\, and student s
 uccess.</p><p>  Viewing party at PAU Center - Bertolini 3rd Floor\, #4832<
 /p><p><strong><a href="https://foundationccc-org.zoom.us/webinar/register/
 WN_j5g13fG9SDyN4njwBP8EUg#/registration" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Re
 gistration though Zoom.</a></strong></p><p><a href="https://dream.santaros
 a.edu/workshops-events-2026-2027" target="_blank" rel="noopener">For more 
 information about Undocumented Student Success Week\, visit the Undocu · 
 Immigrant · Dream Center website.</a></p>
