X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Calendar Livewhale": "https://santarosa.libcal.com/calendar/workshops/noodletools_mla_10_21_26"}
X-SOURCE-ID:calendar_livewhale
SUMMARY:Research Remix: Find Research Cite It Right with NoodleTools @ 4pm
 \, Oct 21st
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T170000
DTSTAMP:20260918T133126Z
UID:20261021T230000Z-24039@calendar.santarosa.edu
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T160000
ATTACH:https://calendar.santarosa.edu/live/image/gid/3/width/80/height/80/
 crop/1/src_region/0,0,1080,1080/644_cs_library_workshop_tour.rev.178605768
 7.png
CATEGORIES:Department Events
DESCRIPTION:Join SRJC Librarian Canon Crawford and learn how to simplify c
 itations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the way\, score quick
  tips on finding credible research in the library and on the Web.NoodleToo
 ls helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliographies\, and offers n
 ote-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\, including the capabi
 lity to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details: Extra Credit availa
 ble!This NoodleTools workshop will use the MLA citation style\, which is t
 ypically used in the English\, ESL\, Humanities\, Philosophy\, and Religio
 n disciplines.If you are using APA\, take this workshop! We will share how
  to choose this option in NoodleTools too.You will learn how to sign up fo
 r an account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to show how to cre
 ate citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.Along the way\,
  you will receive quick tips on how to find credible research in the libra
 ry and on the web.Check with your instructor to confirm the citation style
  appropriate for your research assignment.Extra Credit: As students\, you 
 have the option to submit your instructor and course name when you registe
 r if you would like us to notify your instructor that you have attended th
 e workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an 
 alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.Registration: (clic
 k "Begin Registration" button below)This workshop requires registration in
  order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.You will receive a confirmation 
 email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your spam folder if 
 you do not see it.This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes early to allow y
 ou time to log on.Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC student conduct pol
 icy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how to join a Zoo
 m meeting.Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
LAST-MODIFIED:20260918T213401Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://santarosa.libcal.com/calendar/workshops/noodletools_mla_10_21_
 26
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:Join SRJC Librarian Canon Crawford and learn 
 how to simplify citations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the 
 way\, score quick tips on finding credible research in the library and on 
 the Web.<br />NoodleTools helps you build MLA and APA citations and biblio
 graphies\, and offers note-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features
 \, including the capability to create papers via GoogleDocs.<br />Workshop
  Details: Extra Credit available!<br />This NoodleTools workshop will use 
 the MLA citation style\, which is typically used in the English\, ESL\, Hu
 manities\, Philosophy\, and Religion disciplines.<br />If you are using AP
 A\, take this workshop! We will share how to choose this option in NoodleT
 ools too.<br />You will learn how to sign up for an account with NoodleToo
 ls. We will provide examples to show how to create citations\, create a bi
 bliography and check for errors.<br />Along the way\, you will receive qui
 ck tips on how to find credible research in the library and on the web.<br
  />Check with your instructor to confirm the citation style appropriate fo
 r your research assignment.<br />Extra Credit: As students\, you have the 
 option to submit your instructor and course name when you register if you 
 would like us to notify your instructor that you have attended the worksho
 p for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your instructor on an alternati
 ve way to provide evidence of your attendance.<br />Registration: (click "
 Begin Registration" button below)<br />This workshop requires registration
  in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.<br />You will receive a conf
 irmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your spam f
 older if you do not see it.<br />This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes e
 arly to allow you time to log on.<br />Attendees are asked to abide by SRJ
 C student conduct policy.<br />Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute
  video on how to join a Zoom meeting.<br />Have questions? Chat with an SR
 JC Librarian!
