SUMMARY:Concert Jazz Ensemble & Latin Band
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261022T193000
UID:261001-h2T5N-cFEi861GBmIYy1A
DESCRIPTION:Experience the vibrant fusion of rhythm and improvisation as t
 he Latin Band brings Memo Acevedo’s “Building Bridges\,” Sivuca’s 
 tribute “Um Tom Pra Jobim\,” Jobim’s haunting “Lamento\,” and Ra
 y Obiedo’s lively “Brasileiro” to life\, while the Contemporary Jazz
  Ensemble delivers Tom Harrell’s sleek “Moon Alley\,” a fresh vocal 
 take on Thelonious Monk’s “Ask Me Now\,” Bobby Timmons’s soulful 
 “Moanin’\,” and the lyrical beauty of Kenny Dorham’s “Lotus Blos
 som.” This concert showcases the dynamic interplay between Latin grooves
  and modern jazz sensibilities\, offering students and audiences alike a c
 ompelling journey across musical borders. Don’t miss this unforgettable 
 celebration of cross‑cultural artistry presented by our university’s p
 remier jazz program.
LOCATION:Sonoma State University - Schroeder Hall
URL:https://music.sonoma.edu/events/concert-jazz-ensemble-latin-band-0?utm
 _source=sonoma_calendars&utm_medium=event_calendar&utm_campaign=fall_2026_
 concert_jazz_latin_band_oct22
