DESCRIPTION:HALLOWINE WALK\n\nTrick\, Treat\, & Taste in Yountville\n\nSat
 urday\, October 24\, 2026 12:00 – 4:00 p.m. Washington St. | Yountville\
 n\nCelebrate Halloween with a spirited afternoon in the heart of Yountvill
 e!\n\nJoin us for the inaugural Hallowine Walk: Trick\, Treat & Taste in Y
 ountville\, where wine\, Halloween\, and small-town charm come together fo
 r a one-of-a-kind fall experience.\n\nYour ticket includes a commemorative
  wine cup\, event wristband\, and tasting map. After checking in at Vetera
 ns Memorial Park\, you’ll stroll through Yountville\, visiting participa
 ting wineries\, tasting rooms\, restaurants\, and local businesses while e
 njoying wine tastings\, festive décor\, seasonal surprises\, and exclusiv
 e event-day offerings. \n\nCostumes are encouraged\, so gather your frien
 ds\, dress in your Halloween best\, and enjoy an unforgettable afternoon o
 f wine\, treats\, and festive fun!\n\nTicket Includes:\n\nHallowine Walk c
 up\n\nWine tastings at participating locations\n\nEvent wristband and tast
 ing map\n\nAccess to exclusive event-day specials and promotions\n\nA fest
 ive afternoon exploring downtown Yountville\n\nCheers to a hauntingly good
  time—we can’t wait to see you there!\n\nMust be 21\\+ to participate.
LOCATION:Town of Yountville
URL:https://yountville.com/hallowine-walk/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.frankfamilyvineyards.com/events/simkhai-x-frank-family-vineyards-fashion-show-luncheon-benefiting-dress-for-success", "Press Democrat": "https://www.frankfamilyvineyards.com/events/simkhai-x-frank-family-vineyards-fashion-show-luncheon-benefiting-dress-for-success"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.frankfamilyvineyards.com/events/simkhai-x-frank-family-vineyards-fashion-show-luncheon-benefiting-dress-for-success"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Frank Family X Simkhai Fashion Show & Luncheon Benefiting Dress fo
 r Success
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T120000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T150000
UID:260918coLgyGvTukWrQ_E2T-JB3Q
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an unforgettable afternoon where fashion\, wine\, 
 and philanthropy come together in the heart of Napa Valley.\n\nHosted at F
 rank Family Vineyards\, this exclusive event celebrates our collaboration 
 with Simkhai in support of Dress for Success\, an organization dedicate
 d to empowering women to achieve economic independence through career deve
 lopment\, professional attire\, and a global network of support.\n\nThe ex
 perience begins with a wine reception followed by a beautifully curated mu
 lti-course lunch by Bottega Napa Valley. As guests are seated on our Mill
 er House Lawn\, enjoy an inspiring panel conversation featuring Frank Fami
 ly Founder\, Leslie Frank\, acclaimed fashion designer Jonathan Simkhai\, 
 and Dress for Success CEO Joanie Bily. Together\, they'll discuss the powe
 r of purpose-driven partnerships\, confidence\, and self-expression throug
 h fashion and wine.\n\nGuests will then enjoy an exclusive runway presenta
 tion of the Simkhai pieces\, culminating in the debut of our limited-editi
 on collaborative wine\, created to celebrate craftsmanship\, creativity\, 
 and giving back.\n\nThroughout the afternoon\, renowned color analyst\, T
 he Color Countess\, will offer personalized color analysis sessions\, help
 ing guests discover the colors that best complement their natural features
  while celebrating confidence through personal style.\n\nEvery ticket purc
 hased\, along with a percentage of proceeds from featured wine and Simkhai
  apparel sales during the event\, will directly support Dress for Success 
 and its purpose to help women thrive in work and in life.\n\nWe invite you
  to experience an afternoon of exceptional wine\, inspiring conversation\,
  timeless fashion\, and meaningful impact.
LOCATION:Frank Family Vineyards
URL:https://www.frankfamilyvineyards.com/events/simkhai-x-frank-family-vin
 eyards-fashion-show-luncheon-benefiting-dress-for-success
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
