SUMMARY:Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing at Lynmar Estate
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T123000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T143000
UID:260626HtoYuE_LFEyuKPveUXVhtg
DESCRIPTION:Rooted in the bounty of Quail Hill Vineyard\, Lynmar Estate’
 s Summer Collectors Lunch Pairing invites guests to experience the flavors
  of Sonoma County at their seasonal peak. The elevated four-course menu sh
 owcases ingredients harvested from Lynmar’s organically farmed gardens\,
  orchards\, and olive groves. Each course is individually plated and thoug
 htfully paired with Lynmar’s acclaimed estate-grown Pinot Noirs\, Chardo
 nnays\, and sparkling wines\, creating a journey that is both deeply conne
 cted to Sonoma County and globally inspired. Served in the idyllic setting
  of Quail Hill Vineyard\, the experience is further enhanced by a special 
 tableside visit from Estate Chef David Frakes.\n\nCollectors Lunch Pairing
  Menu Summer 2026:\n\nAdam’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nWarm Organic 
 Popcorn\n\nWhite Corn-Kasundi Salt\, Estate Extra-Virgin Olive Oil\n\nSusa
 nna’s Vineyard Chardonnay\, 2022\n\nThai Green Curry & Coconut Soup\n\nB
 liss Snap Peas & Heirloom Radish\n\nYoung Vines Pinot Noir\, 2021\n\nHeirl
 oom Potato & Cherry Tomato ‘Croustade’\n\nSmoked Bacon-Grain Mustard D
 ressing\n\nSusanna’s Vineyard Pinot Noir\, 2022\n\nRoasted Syrian Seven-
 Spiced Chicken Breast\n\nIndonesian Corn Fritter\, Summer Vegetable Ragout
 \, Balado Sauce\n\nRosé de Blancs Sparkling\, 2021\n\nChilled Vanilla Bur
 nt Basque Cheesecake\n\nRaspberry-Rose Syrup\, Black Tea & Licorice-Poache
 d Cherries\n\nBrown Butter Nilla Cookie\, Candied Lime\n\nEstate Ingredien
 ts:\n\nBay Laurel\, Cherries\, Chives\, Edible Flowers\, Lemons\, Olive Oi
 l\, Peas\, Potatoes\, Radishes\, Raspberries\, Thyme\, Tomatoes\, Zucchini
  and more!\n\nMenu by Estate Chef David Frakes\n\nReservations are require
 d. Maximum group size is six guests.
LOCATION:Lynmar Estate
URL:https://lynmarestate.com/reservation/type/collectors-lunch-pairing/ 
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
