BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Haunted Wine Tour & Tasting
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T173000
UID:260831htVfNX3h9E6wXKnSBxz6tA
DESCRIPTION:This fall\, Buena Vista Winery invites you to uncover the myst
 eries\, legends\, and ghostly encounters woven into more than 165 years of
  history. Led by Sonoma historian and actor George Webber\, this immersive
  90 minute experience journeys through the historic Press House and Champa
 gne Cellars\, revealing true tales of unexplained happenings reported by B
 uena Vista team members and visitors throughout the years.\n\nHear the sto
 ries of the Glowing Ghostly Shirt\, the Little Girl Who Says Hi\, the myst
 erious Ghost Party on the Second Floor\, the Old Man Who Walked Into a Sto
 ne Wall\, and other strange occurrences that continue to add to the legend
  of Buena Vista.\n\nAlong the way\, explore some of the winery’s most in
 triguing spaces\, including the Bubble Lounge\, Cave of Curiosities\, and 
 Wine Tool Museum\, while enjoying five Buena Vista wines tasted throughout
  the experience\, including a taste drawn directly from barrel.\n\nAnd\, a
 s with any journey through Buena Vista’s extraordinary past\, you never 
 quite know when the winery’s legendary founder\, Count Agoston Haraszthy
 \, may choose to make an appearance.\n\nHistory\, wine\, mystery\, and per
 haps a spirit or two await.
LOCATION:Buena Vista Historical Winery
URL:https://eventvesta.com/events/160340/t/tickets
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/whistler", "Press Democrat": "https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/whistler"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/whistler"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Documentary:  JAMES McNEIL WHISTLER
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261024T173000
UID:260823DiQLVhHiV0WLp6tCOzlFFQ
DESCRIPTION:Whistler was a loud and fascinating character who lived life t
 o the full. But above all\, and despite all the legal scandals and verbal 
 posturing\, he was a magnificent painter\, printmaker and writer. An extre
 mely proficient and imaginative artist with a gift for creativity and expr
 ession that embraced the cult of beauty\, pushed the boundaries of paintin
 g and gave birth to modern art. \n\nTate Britain is now holding the first
  major retrospective of Whistler in three decades. This blockbuster exhibi
 tion promises to reawaken the world to just how important Whistler is to a
 rt history\, uniting world-famous masterpieces with rarely seen works. Exh
 ibition on Screen will bring these stunning works and the incredible story
  behind them to cinemas around the world while the exhibition is still run
 ning\, bringing this truly global artist to a global audience. This will b
 e an unmissable chance to get to know this visually spectacular artist and
  the influence he has had on those who followed.
LOCATION:Jarvis Conservatory
URL:https://jarvisconservatory.ticketspice.com/whistler
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
