BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.notloudconcerts.com/", "Press Democrat": "https://www.notloudconcerts.com/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://www.notloudconcerts.com/"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Napa $5 Folk Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T170000
UID:260930Au7mnPaIJ0WJrYFp5Yr-0g
DESCRIPTION:A $5 music festival in Napa? That’s right! \n\nNot Loud Con
 certs presents the Napa $5 Folk Festival on Oct 25 from 2 - 5 pm.\n\nThis 
 is a festival like no other - 9 bands\, 3 stages\, all indoors in downtown
  Napa\, and all not too loud! Stroll between the stages hearing amazing in
 ternationally touring bands\, local favorites\, and a few surprises. Prese
 nted by Not Loud Concerts\, this event takes out all of the hassles and di
 scomfort of modern music festivals and puts the audience and musician's co
 mfort first. Best of all\, admission is only $5.\n\nThe festival is held e
 ntirely indoors in the historic Native Sons of the Gold West (on Coombs)\,
  in multiple rooms on a couple of different floors. Large bands will be fe
 atured in the grand ballroom\, acoustic-based bands will perform intimate 
 sets in the wood paneled meeting room\, and in the dance room there will b
 e folk dancing lessons and some surprise acts.\n\nIndoor bathrooms\, chair
 s to sit in\, room to dance and\, of course\, sound reinforcement that is 
 not too loud make this festival one of a kind. All of this for just $5.\n\
 nThere is lots of nearby\, free\, parking and there are elevators in the h
 all\, along with chairs in every room. The friendly folks at the Native So
 ns Hall will have drinks for sale.\n\nBuying tickets in advance is recomme
 nded (and appreciated)\, but tickets will also be for sale at the door.\n\
 nCheck out the amazing bands.\n\nDirty Cello - internationally touring blu
 egrass and blues band\n\nLaurie Lewis - one of the founders of California 
 bluegrass music\n\nFrog Face Band - Americana and bluegrass band\n\nCoyote
  Slim - traditional blues and old time folk songs with humorous stories\n\
 nCosmo and Leslie - a local bluesy folk rock duo\n\nClementine Darling - a
 n indie folk/americana musician\n\nLovejack - cellist playing Bridgerton -
  like arrangements of modern songs\n\nLindsay Everly - Americana singer-so
 ngwriter \n\nFolk dancing lessons from Marian Snyder of Berkeley Folk Dan
 ce\n\nNapa $5 Folk Festival\n\nNative Sons of the Golden West\n\n927 Coomb
 s St\, Napa\, CA 94559\n\nOct 25 from 2 - 5 pm\n\nTickets: $5 at NotLoudCo
 ncerts.com
LOCATION:Native Sons of the Golden West
URL:https://www.notloudconcerts.com/
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://bricoleurvineyards.com/blogs/events/sculpt-sip-with-purpose"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Sculpt & Sip with Purpose
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261025T160000
UID:260929RwMHBQx6ikKHmHm8zAn25w
DESCRIPTION:Join us at Bricoleur Vineyards for an afternoon celebrating Br
 east Cancer Awareness Month\, held in honor of our "Sip with Purpose" camp
 aign. We're excited to partner with Social Wellness Society\, Sutter Healt
 h\, Drink DUJU and more to bring you a meaningful afternoon of movement\, 
 connection\, and celebration - all in support of a great cause. 100% of ti
 cket sales will be donated to the V Foundation for Cancer Research\, suppo
 rting life-saving research and giving hope to families everywhere.\n\nThe 
 event will kick off with a 45-minute Pilates and sculpt class led by Justi
 ne Licursi of Social Wellness Society\, setting the tone for an afternoon 
 centered on strength\, wellness\, and community.Following class\, guests w
 ill enjoy a glass of our beloved Isla Rose Brut Rosé while mingling with 
 fellow supporters in the beauty of Bricoleur Vineyards. Hear directly from
  Sarah Citron as she shares her personal journey with breast cancer and th
 e profound impact of the V Foundation's support along the way.This afterno
 on is made even more special thanks to our generous vendor partners: Falli
 ng for Dainty will be on-site selling beautiful jewelry donating 15% of sa
 les to the cause. Sarah with Bloom Event Co has generously donated stunnin
 g florals and Nothing Bundt Cakes has donated delicious desserts for all t
 o enjoy.\n\nEvery guest will also take home a gift bag valued at over $300
  — our way of saying thank you for standing with us in the fight against
  cancer.Come move\, sip\, celebrate\, and support a cause that touches so 
 many of us. Together\, we can make a meaningful difference.\n\nEvent Detai
 ls:\n\n• Includes: 45 minute mat pilates and sculpt class \\*Please brin
 g your own yoga mat\, as they are not provided.\n\n• Timing: 2:00pm - 4:
 00pm \\*Please note this will be held outdoors.• Availability: Limited -
  50 spots available\n\n• Club Members: Club discounts do not apply.\n\n
 • Dress Code: Pilates or workout clothing\, dressing in pink is encourag
 ed\n\n• Age Requirement: 21\\+ only\n\n• Pets: Not permitted at this e
 vent
LOCATION:Bricoleur Vineyard
URL:https://bricoleurvineyards.com/blogs/events/sculpt-sip-with-purpose
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian
END:VEVENT
