DESCRIPTION:Tuesday\, October 27\, 2026\n\n6:00pm    Doors open 5:30 pm\
 n\nFree entry. Donations greatly appreciated.\n\nConcessions open for purc
 hase.\n\nAssistive listening devices available.\n\n Sponsored by Deanna M
 adeson\n\nIn this noir classic\, detective Sam Spade \\(Humphrey Bogart\\)
  gets more than he bargained for when he takes a case brought to him by a 
 beautiful but secretive woman \\(Mary Astor\\). As soon as Miss Wonderly s
 hows up\, trouble follows as Sam's partner is murdered and Sam is accosted
  by a man \\(Peter Lorre\\) demanding he locate a valuable statuette. Sam\
 , entangled in a dangerous web of crime and intrigue\, soon realizes he mu
 st find the one thing they all seem to want: the bejeweled Maltese falcon.
 \n\n Released Oct 18\, 1941\n\nCrime\, Drama\n\nRuntime 1h 40m
LOCATION:Soper-Reese Theatre
