X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/aspooky2026", "Press Democrat": "https://sec.regfox.com/aspooky2026", "Visit Santa Rosa": "https://www.visitsantarosa.com/events/a-spooky-autumn-nature-hike/"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://sec.regfox.com/aspooky2026"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:A “Spooky” Autumn Nature Hike
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T130000
UID:260926fxJgwEZ2aUaJ-CIW6jrIZw
DESCRIPTION:Join Certified California Naturalist John Lynch on a 
 “spooky” 3 mile\, 3.5 hour hike from Creekside to Hillside a
 nd back through the meadow exploring this very special season. \
 n\nWith Halloween around the corner\, we might just discover witc
 hes' butter\, flying saucer galls\, zombie leaves\, plants that h
 ave been skeletonized\, or even some “ghostly“ sheet web spid
 ers. Have the bats been using their bat house\, let’s find ou
 t. We’ll also see if we can identify some of the “treats”
  of the season (seeds\, nuts\, and berries) and the plants that
  produce them. Oh\, and of course\, spooky stories.\n\nTickets ar
 e $10 for general audiences\, $5 for youth (12-17 year olds)\, 
 students\, Sugarloaf members\, Sugarloaf volunteers\, and free for
  children under 12. All minors must be accompanied by a parent
  or legal guardian. Meet at the White Barn parking lot. Bring 
 at least a quart of water\, sun protection\, wear appropriate cl
 othing and footwear for slippery and rocky trails\, and if desir
 ed\, a snack. Parking fees apply. Heavy rains cancel.
LOCATION:Sugarloaf Ridge State Park
URL:https://sec.regfox.com/aspooky2026
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat, Visit Santa Rosa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/love-loss-and-letting-go-vf1d26/?lang=en", "Press Democrat": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/love-loss-and-letting-go-vf1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"North Bay Bohemian": "https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/love-loss-and-letting-go-vf1d26/?lang=en"}
X-SOURCE-ID:bohemian
SUMMARY:Love\, Loss\, and Letting Go
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T130000
UID:260817m364mM_tmUm9pGbB-feFJw
DESCRIPTION:with Vinny Ferraro and Frank Ostaseski\n\nThere is no getting 
 through a human life without loss. The question is not whether we will be 
 asked to let go\, but how we will meet what must be let go. In this half-d
 ay\, we’ll explore how practice can help us meet grief\, love\, and impe
 rmanence without turning away. Together we’ll reflect on how to meet bot
 h the suffering of the world and the more intimate losses of our own lives
  with honesty\, care\, and courage.\n\nThis is not about transcending grie
 f or arriving at some perfected acceptance. It’s about what helps us sta
 y open\, present\, and human when life asks us to let go.\n\nFor alumni an
 d current Year to Live folks in the Bay Area\, this serves as a long-await
 ed reunion—a rare opportunity to be together in person! For those curiou
 s about the Year to Live journey\, it offers a little taste of the practic
 e container and a chance to meet Vinny and Frank—either onsite or online
 . Join us to reflect more deeply on letting go and on appreciating the lif
 e that is here now.
LOCATION:Spirit Rock Meditation Center
URL:https://spirit-rock.secure.retreat.guru/program/love-loss-and-letting-
 go-vf1d26/?lang=en
X-SOURCE:North Bay Bohemian, Press Democrat
END:VEVENT
