DESCRIPTION:Join SRJC Librarian Jessica Harris and learn how to simplify c
 itations using the "NoodleTools" citation app. Along the way\, score quick
  tips on finding credible research in the library and on the Web.NoodleToo
 ls helps you build MLA and APA citations and bibliographies\, and offers n
 ote-taking\, outlining\, and paper-writing features\, including the capabi
 lity to create papers via GoogleDocs.Workshop Details: Extra Credit availa
 ble!This NoodleTools workshop will use APA and/or MLA style as live demo e
 xamples\, depending on the participants that register.Don't worry! Jessica
  will share how to use both MLA and APA. You're covered!You will learn how
  to sign up for an account with NoodleTools. We will provide examples to s
 how how to create citations\, create a bibliography and check for errors.A
 long the way\, you will receive quick tips on how to find credible researc
 h in the library and on the web.Check with your instructor to confirm the 
 citation style appropriate for your research assignment.Extra Credit: As s
 tudents\, you have the option to submit your instructor and course name wh
 en you register if you would like us to notify your instructor that you ha
 ve attended the workshop for extra credit. Or\, you can work with your ins
 tructor on an alternative way to provide evidence of your attendance.Regis
 tration: (click "Begin Registration" button below)This workshop requires r
 egistration in order to be admitted to the Zoom meeting.You will receive a
  confirmation email with the Zoom URL link for this workshop. Check your s
 pam folder if you do not see it.This Zoom workshop will open 10 minutes ea
 rly to allow you time to log on.Attendees are asked to abide by SRJC stude
 nt conduct policy.Not familiar with Zoom? Watch this 1-minute video on how
  to join a Zoom meeting.Have questions? Chat with an SRJC Librarian!
LAST-MODIFIED:20261005T200028Z
LOCATION:Online
URL:https://santarosa.libcal.com/calendar/workshops/noodletools_mla_11_9_2
