X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Crafting a Recycled Eco-Petal Bouquet  — Sebastopol Center For t
 he Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261114T000000
DTEND:20261115T000000
UID:a6268fff8ee3445d75c49be4fb9ffab4@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Eco Petals: Crafting a Recycled Bouquet\n\n  \n    \n      \n 
        \n          $70.00\n        \n      \n    \n  \n\nSaturday\, Novemb
 er 14th\, 1:00-4:00pm$60 + $10 Materials feeAges 13+Create a whimsical upc
 ycled bouquet using imagination and an assortment of found and recycled pa
 pers. In this playful workshop\, you’ll learn simple techniques for shap
 ing paper flowers and combining colors\, textures\, and unexpected materia
 ls. No experience needed—just come ready to explore and leave with a one
 -of-a-kind handmade bouquet. All supplies provided.About the Instructor: R
 endell Hourigan received a BBA in Marketing from Texas Tech University\, a
 nd has pursued art for over 25 years\, focusing on sustainable mixed media
 . She has studied with artists including Chery Baird\, Jenny London\, and 
 Teri Sloat\, exploring drawing\, collage\, and soft pastels. Her training 
 includes workshops and courses in art journaling\, mosaics\, and mark-maki
 ng. She’s exhibited work at the Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, The Gra
 ton Gallery\, and her SOFA district studio. Drawn to the beauty of discard
 ed materials and passionate about recycling\, she incorporates reclaimed m
 aterials into her work and now leads art workshops to inspire eco-consciou
 s creativity in others.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n            \n              \n                A
 dd to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/crafting-a-recycled-eco-petal
 -bouquet
