 a toward dignity\, agency\, and self-representation. The women within thes
 e pages are dancers\, artists\, beadworkers\, teachers\, mothers\, daughte
 rs\, grandmothers\, language keepers\, and land and water defenders. They 
 are culture bearers\, but they are not defined by what they carry for othe
 rs." — Julian Cook\, Co-Creator</p><p><em>This project is funded by a gr
 ant from the Santa Rosa Junior College Foundation Randolph Newman Cultural
  Enrichment Endowment.</em></p><p><a href="https://museum.santarosa.edu/ev
 ent/standing-her-power-portraits-beyond-colonial-frame" target="_blank" re
 l="noopener">For more information\, visit the SRJC Multicultural Museum we
 bsite.</a></p>
