SUMMARY:WALKING MIRRORS Benefitting Dominican University of California
DESCRIPTION:Dinner Show with WALKING MIRRORS\nFeaturing:\nCraig Bartock (Rock n Roll Hall of Fame Band Heart)\nDavid Sikes (former decade long bass player/vocalist/songwriter for rock n roll band BOSTON)\nJeff Campitelli (50th Greatest Drummer of all-time: Rolling Stone) \n“For me\, our music is a creative collaboration of stories that musically connect to community.  Stories that reflect what is going on in the world today and resonate in an ear pleasing way. Playing that music live with some of the top musicians in the Bay Area (Craig Bartock-Heart\, Jeff Campitelli- formerly with Joe Satriani\, David Sikes- formerly with Boston) is surreal. Add my guitar shredding son Aidan\, and it is like playing in a dream” \nMark Nelson\, Lead Singer and Songwriter
URL:https://ranchonicasio.com/event/walking-mirrors-benefitting-dominican-university-of-california/
LOCATION:Rancho Nicasio\, 1 Old Rancheria Rd\, Nicasio\, CA\, 94946\, United States
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://ranchonicasio.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/584324.jpeg
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE-URLS:{"Sebastopol Center for the Arts": "https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/jizo-peace-project-clay-gathering-for-remembrance-and-peace-december"}
X-SOURCE-ID:sebarts
SUMMARY:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering for Remembrance and Peace\, Dec
 ember — Sebastopol Center For the Arts\, California
DTSTART:20261204T000000
DTEND:20261205T000000
UID:2e7d9430b66a4c2a2719c408b5274976@sebarts.org
DESCRIPTION:Jizo Peace Project: Clay Gathering for Remembrance and Peace\,
  December\n\n  \n    \n      \n        \n          $10.00\n        \n     
  \n    \n  \n\nFriday\, December 4\, 2026\; 1:30 – 4:00pmDue to limited 
 capacity\, we are asking for a suggested donation of $10 to the Sebastopol
  Center for the Arts to confirm your attendance. Bring a copy of your rece
 ipt at check-in to Painting/Drawing Studio adjacent to Ceramics Studio. Ad
 ditional donations are welcome at the time of the class to cover rental an
 d expenses for the peace project. Join us for a monthly\, heart-centered g
 athering where we come together to create Jizo guardians out of clay—sym
 bols of compassion\, protection\, and peace. Rooted in the Buddhist tradit
 ion and echoed across many cultures\, Jizo figures traditionally honor chi
 ldren and all who have passed\, those in transition\, and those in distres
 s.This ongoing project is dedicated to remembering those lost to war\, wit
 h a special focus now on the approximately 19\,000 children who have peris
 hed in Israel and Gaza in recent years. Through the simple\, meditative ac
 t of working with clay\, we create benevolent beings that will become part
  of public exhibits and peace sites\, offering spaces for reflection\, mou
 rning\, and hope. Our gatherings conclude with a gentle ritual to honor th
 e lives of these children.Located in the Painting & Drawing Room. The gath
 ering is open to ages 12 - adult\, and no prior clay experience is necessa
 ry—all clay and basic materials are supplied. Registration is required t
 o participate.Donations are welcome to help cover materials and expenses. 
 More than a class\, this is a shared space of warmth and care—an opportu
 nity to tend to our own hearts while taking part in love in action.\n\n\n\
 n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n          \n   
          \n              \n                Add to cart
LOCATION:Sebastopol Center for the Arts\, 282 S High St\, Sebastopol\, CA 
 95472
URL:https://www.sebarts.org/classes-lectures/jizo-peace-project-clay-gathe
 ring-for-remembrance-and-peace-december
X-SOURCE:Sebastopol Center for the Arts
END:VEVENT
